Z||000000||My7Fieros||02-25-2001||01:33 AM||||Is the oil sending unit different on an 88(V6) than on the other years? Reason I ask is because Ive changed them all..and (the only) 88 I have the oil sending unit is much smaller than on the others. Courious, thanx.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||2
Z||000001||terryk||02-25-2001||12:01 PM||||There are several versions of the senders, but they have some common pieces. Yes, they also vary in packages.<P>For the oil sender, there is the switch version for the idiot light or pot version (0-90 ohms) for the gauge. <P>Then an additional switch may be added for the fuel pump override. <P>Some have common wiring, other are seperate.<P>They all generally interchange. Around 88, GM switched to a new type that was more slender. Maybe that's what you are seeing.<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 02-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Black88GT||02-25-2001||02:37 PM||||Yeah the oil sensor is different on '88s, not sure exactly how though.||||reg||1
